    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i had surgery on my left knee like 5 days ago and i'm doing okay mostly but my calf is getting really swollen and it feels kind of tight and sore. is that just normal swelling from the surgery or should i be worried? my other leg looks fine it's just the one.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's not uncommon to experience some swelling, tightness, and soreness after surgery, so this may be normal. However, you should monitor for any changes in the size or shape of the swelling, any increase in pain, and discoloration. If the changes persist or bother you, I would recommend contacting your healthcare provider for a follow-up examination and advice. Keeping your knee elevated and applying ice might help in the meantime.",
